page RecipeDeployToVercel(path: "/recipes/deploy-to-vercel", title: "Deploy to Vercel — Recipes", description: "1.") {
    RecipeShell("Deploy to Vercel", summary: "1. Add `vercel.json` at the project's root:     ```json \{ \"buildCommand\": \"curl -sSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/monzeromer-lab/WebFluent/master/install.sh | bash && ~/.webfluent/bin/wf build\", \"outputDirectory\": \"build\", \"headers\": [ \{ \"source\": \"/(.*)\", \"headers\": [ \{ \"key\": \"X-Content-Type-Options\", \"value\": \"nosniff\" \}, \{ \"key\": \"Referrer-Policy\", \"value\": \"strict-origin-when-cross-origin\" \}, \{ \"key\": \"X-Frame-Options\", \"value\": \"DENY\" \} ] \} ] \} ```  2. Vercel does not read `_headers`. Copy every header the build wrote in `build/_headers` into `headers`, including the `Content-Security-Policy` line. 3. For a single-page build, add `\"rewrites\": [\{ \"source\": \"/(.*)\", \"destination\": \"/index.html\" \}]`.  **Verify it:** compare the response headers in the network panel with `build/_headers`. Each header in the file should be there.", outputs: [], since: "", recipes: RECIPE_INDEX, sections: [], related: [RelatedLink(kind: "Recipe", title: "Build a Docker image", to: "/recipes/docker-image"), RelatedLink(kind: "Recipe", title: "Check a deploy", to: "/recipes/check-a-deploy"), RelatedLink(kind: "Recipe", title: "Deploy to Cloudflare Pages", to: "/recipes/deploy-to-cloudflare-pages")], source: "md-docs/recipes/deploy-to-vercel.md", how: false, hasVariations: false) {
    }
}
